== ARCHIVE: CCSD(T) counterpoise anchor extended from one system to three (6-31g*) ==

Why: section 3.2 of paper/main.md reported the counterpoise-corrected interaction energy for
six systems and the only correlated anchor was the water dimer, so the comparison was
asymmetric - ammonia (-3.675) and methane (-0.466) sit in the same table with nothing to
check them against. This run adds both, same basis (6-31g*), same functional-free method
stack (RHF reference, MP2/CCSD/CCSD(T) from PySCF), same counterpoise convention
(E_complex - sum of halves each in its own basis at the complex geometry), same official S22
initial geometries (S22_02 / S22_01 / S22_08), same frozen-core rule (one 1s per heavy atom
on both sides of the difference, from a single freeze_plan() call).

Run: OMP_NUM_THREADS=16 BASES="6-31g*" SYSTEMS="水二聚体,氨二聚体,甲烷二聚体"
     PYTHONPATH=. python3 -u nlcsplit/step_m_ccsdt.py     (PySCF 2.12.1, Python 3.10.12, EXIT=0)

Dimer sizes printed by the run: water nao=36 (2x18), ammonia nao=40 (2x20), methane nao=44 (2x22);
all three with nelec=20 and a frozen count of 2 on the complex / 1+1 on the halves.

Regression check that comes free: the water row of this three-system run is
-7.149 / -6.682 / -6.856 / -6.887 (MP2 / CCSD / CCSD(T) / all-electron), identical to the
values in `20260930T224400Z_stepm_ladder_after_refactor.out`. The generalisation to multiple
systems moved no number.

What the three rows say together, and what they do not say:

  system    MP2     CCSD    CCSD(T)   all-electron   our wB97X-V CP (level 2)
  water    -7.149  -6.682   -6.856       -6.887            -6.129
  ammonia  -4.620  -4.293   -4.455       -4.473            -3.675
  methane  -0.149  -0.129   -0.178       -0.187            -0.466

At fixed basis the functional is *shallower* than correlation on the two hydrogen-bonded
systems (by 0.73 and 0.78 kcal/mol) and *deeper* on the methane dimer (by 0.29). The sign
of the discrepancy is system-dependent, which is a stronger and less convenient statement
than the single water row could support.

The methane row must NOT be read as evidence about the functional yet: 6-31g* has no
diffuse functions, and the methane dimer is dispersion-bound, so its correlated value
(-0.178 kcal/mol) is a basis artefact as much as a physical number. A companion run in
aug-cc-pVDZ is archived separately; if the sign of the methane deviation does not survive
that basis, the sentence in section 3.2 says so rather than keeping the convenient reading.

